                        "glosses": [
                            "A shapeshifter who can assume the form of a hare."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9975bd32-4c3f-4331-97d5-352f1d138c72",
                                "sense_id": "2fcfe6b2-543c-3b63-b441-f6ac90707ed6",
                                "text": "“‘Oh my,’ cried the first camper. ‘Now I understand you completely. You've turned into a werehare!’"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e7d6fcc4-1598-4e59-b4d6-a51e018d3162",
                                "sense_id": "2fcfe6b2-543c-3b63-b441-f6ac90707ed6",
                                "text": "Like all the children in the neighborhood, A____ and Z____ had grown up hearing strange stories about the Were-Hare, the monster rabbit who allegedly haunted the woods behind their street. According to legend, the Were-Hare had teeth of gold, so long they reached below his chin. Anybody bitten by the Were-Hare went mad—and believed for the rest of his life he was a rodent in human form. On the other hand, anybody who managed to extract one of the Were-Hare's teeth would have good luck for as long as he could keep the tooth."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6ec46a88-b64a-40b8-8306-975b6503ac61",
                                "sense_id": "2fcfe6b2-543c-3b63-b441-f6ac90707ed6",
                                "text": "\"Maybe it wasn't the Seeing Hare at all, maybe it was a person in hare form. A were-hare. Look, I don't know!\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4806df3b-ca3b-4076-a4eb-41e182d80e16",
                                "sense_id": "2fcfe6b2-543c-3b63-b441-f6ac90707ed6",
                                "text": "If he hadn't know better, he'd have thought she was a werehare, something that lived to nibble grass and hide. Not the infuriated creature who had nearly killed a werewolf in his prime."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
